Subject: The profiler records an element store the compiled inline store would not take

What this does
  - `AOT_PROF_PUT` in `regvm_t_put_element` and `regvm_t_put_element_xfer` (profile builds
    only; empty otherwise) sets `AOT_ELEM_HOLEY` on the store's pc when the receiver is not an
    array or typed array with an existing, non-hole element at the key, i.e. the store grows
    the array or fills a hole.

Why we need it
  A frameless compiled body can only leave at a miss. A leaf that fills a fresh `new Array(n)`
  (earleyboyer's `sc_vectorFillBang`) missed on its first store of every call and was switched
  off by the 257-exit rule. The generator now keeps such a function framed.

